meta {
  name: Upload Report
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

put {
  url: {{reconUploadUrl}}
  body: file
  auth: none
}

body:file {
  file: @file(fixtures/dash-new-business-demo.xlsx) @contentType(application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet)
}

tests {
  test("storage accepts the upload", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  # PUT <uploadUrl> — the raw report (step 2 of 3)

  Not an API endpoint: this goes **straight to object storage** with the URL
  from `Presign Upload`. `auth: none` — the collection's bearer would break
  the S3 signature.

  ## The fixture

  `bruno/fixtures/dash-new-business-demo.xlsx` is a synthetic Dash export laid
  out like the real one (metadata rows, then the 25-column header). Invented
  names; the policy numbers are the demo seed's (`9002000NN`), so lines match:

  | Line | What it exercises |
  |---|---|
  | 900200000, 900200002 | matched, credited to the producer who sold it |
  | 900200004 | matched, but Dash credits Pat where the app credits Morgan |
  | 900299990 | in Dash, not in the app |
  | 900299991 (Bind ID `OSCVANJ`, 1-800) | 1-800 review |
  | 900200005 (add item) | not new business |
  | Motor Club line | never reconciled |

  It carries **no agent number**, on purpose: `Carrier Appointments` gives
  the demo agency a new random Allstate code every run, so a fixed number
  would be refused as another agency's report. The run warns instead.

  ⚠ `Presign Upload` and `Create Run` declare the file's size (**24069**
  bytes). Regenerating the fixture means updating both.
}
